extends RefCounted
## Authored pull requests. "before" is the file already on main (absent for a new
## file); "lines" is the proposed version. Both are clean under every standard;
## faults are applied by policy_campaign.gd. Lines stay within sixty columns.
##
## Order is the campaign arc: entries escalate from office absurdity (days 1-5)
## through AI-first mandates, surveillance, layoffs-as-features, and Helios
## taking over the review desk. The first 150 fill ten days of fifteen; later
## entries are spares in the same register.
##
## Author dialogue: one plain String per field (not a per-author dictionary).
## Each line is written to work whether Maya, Theo, or June wrote the PR. Lines
## stay under 70 characters, with no exclamation marks, and never name a rule
## ID or what a standard checks for:
##   pitch     what the author says when the PR reaches your desk
##   pushback  disputing a change request; never hints whether the PR is broken
##   relief    on approval
##   grudge    abandoning or escalating after being sent back
## Readers should still fall back to generic banter if a field is missing.

